# Cloudflare Pages reads this file and applies it to static responses; it is never
# served itself. It mirrors the headers set in site/server/src/main.rs, so the page
# behaves identically whether the Rust binary or Pages is in front of it.
#
# The mechanism that shapes this file: matching rules INHERIT rather than override.
# A request that matches two patterns receives both rules' headers, so writing
# Cache-Control twice would emit it twice rather than replace it. A more specific
# rule therefore deletes the inherited value with "! " before setting its own.

# connect-src and form-action are 'self' because the subscribe modal posts to our
# own /api/subscribe. Without connect-src the fetch would be blocked by our own
# policy, since it falls back to default-src 'none'.
#
# img-src carries data: for one reason, the grain: styles.css tiles an inlined
# feTurbulence SVG as a background-image, and a data: URI is an image source like any
# other, so img-src 'self' alone refused it. Found 2026-09-03 in a headless browser,
# after the grain had already shipped: "Loading the image 'data:image/svg+xml,...'
# violates the following Content Security Policy directive: img-src 'self'". Nobody saw
# it in a curl, because a curl does not render. data: cannot execute anything under
# img-src; the tighter alternative is to serve the SVG as a real file, which is a build
# change rather than a header change.
#
# The two cloudflareinsights.com entries are Web Analytics, which is enabled on the
# Pages project and injected at the edge, after the build, into every HTML response
# that looks like it came from a browser. It needs both: static.cloudflareinsights.com
# to load beacon.min.js, and cloudflareinsights.com to POST the page view back. While
# script-src was 'self' alone the browser refused the injected script, so the setting
# was on in the dashboard and dead on the page. A policy that silently blocks a
# measurement you believe you are taking is worse than not measuring, because the
# dashboard still shows a number and the number is of nothing.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# Only /assets/ carries content hashes, so only /assets/ may promise immutability:
# a change there produces a new filename, never a new body under an old name.
# Everything else (the HTML, theme.js, anim.js, favicon.svg) keeps the Pages default
# of "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate", which revalidates on every request exactly
# as the binary's "no-cache" does, and answers 304 from the ETag when nothing moved.
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
